s neck.\n\n- Input Edit Put the convertible on an empty desert road under a clear sky.\n\n- Input Edit Add a small caravan of three camels along the dune ridge.\n\n- Input Edit Add broad crimson stripes across the sails.\n\n## Commercial weights\n\nRunning FLUX 3 Image Klein in a product? A commercial license covers self-hosted deployment at scale. Reach out to us to learn more.\n\n## Start building with FLUX 3 Image Klein.\n\nDownload the weights, read the license, and run it on your own hardware.\n\n### What is FLUX 3 Image Klein?\n\nFLUX 3 Image Klein is the open-weights member of the FLUX 3 Image family. It generates images from text, edits them from an instruction and combines several references into one image, all in a single model you download and run on your own hardware.\n\n### How do I use it?\n\nDownload the weights from Hugging Face and run them in your own pipeline, or wire the model into ComfyUI or your own stack. The docs cover setup, prompting and layouts with bounding boxes. Read the docs\n\n### Can I place elements with bounding boxes?\n\nYes. Give each element a box and a description, and Klein renders it inside that box. The canvas is a 0 to 1000 grid on both axes, whatever the aspect ratio, and each box is written as [y_min, x_min, y_max, x_max].\n\n### Can I fine-tune it?\n\nYes. The weights are yours to fine-tune, distill and build on, within the terms of the license they come with.\n\n### What license are the weights under?\n\nThe open weights come with the license on their Hugging Face model card. Read it before you use them; the licensing page explains how our model licenses fit together. Licensing\n\n### Can I use FLUX 3 Image Klein in a commercial product?\n\nRunning Klein in a product needs a commercial license, which covers self-hosted deployment at scale. Talk to us about the terms. Contact sales"
